1
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Dem baş temaşevanên me yên hêja û temaşevanên me yên ezîz.
 
Good day, our dear and esteemed viewers.

2
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Em gihiştin vê deştê, şemal di serî me da xist, me zanîbû
tiştekî Efrînî heye.
 
We reached this plain, the breeze hit our head, we knew
there was an Afrin thing.

3
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Gava ez hatim ji Cûqê, di nav baxçeyan, di nav xwedanên Cûqê
da, şemalekî Efrînî di serî min xist.
 
When I came from Cuqe, among the orchards, among the owners
of Cuqe, an Afrin breeze hit my head.

4
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Û îro em derbasî gundê Baedîna dibin, di gundê Baedîna jî em
ê derbasî malbatekê bibin.
 
And today we are entering the village of Baedina, and in the
village of Baedina we will visit a family.

5
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Ev malbat jî, malbata Mihemed e... xalê Mihemed yê bavê
Rêber.
 
And this family, is Muhammad's family... Uncle Muhammad,
Reber's father.

6
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Silavê me ji kekê Rêber re jî heye, hevalê me ye, wekî bira
ye.
 
We send our greetings to brother Reber too, he is our
friend, like a brother.

7
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Îro em ê derbasî cem xalê Mihemed bibin, em ê rojeke Efrînî
bêtir bi hev re derbas bikin.
 
Today we will visit Uncle Muhammad, we will spend a more
Afrin day together.

8
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Temaşevanên me yên hêja, tiştên berê gelekî xweş bûn, û pir
xweş bûn.
 
Our dear viewers, the things of the past were very
beautiful, and very pleasant.

9
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Nemaze bîranînên berê, bav û kalên me genim dikelandin, em
zarok bûn, me zikê xwe dida ber genimê kelandî.
 
Especially the old memories, our ancestors boiled wheat, we
were kids, we would eat the boiled wheat until we were full.

10
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Lê îro, em ê dîsa derbasî cem bavê Rêber bibin, xalê
Mihemed.
 
But today, we will again visit Reber's father, Uncle
Muhammad.

11
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Em ê bi hev re lê binêrin, xalê Mihemed, sal bi sal, ji
destpêkê ta dawiyê di hewşa xwe de genim dikelîne.
 
We will see together, Uncle Muhammad, year by year, from
start to finish in his yard boils wheat.

12
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Piştî genim keland, radixe...
 
After boiling the wheat, he spreads it...

13
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Bi destê xwe... xudê temenê wan dirêj bike.
 
With his own hands... may God give them a long life.

14
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Bi gundiyan û xanimên gundiyan û zarokên gundiyan.
 
With the villagers and the women of the villagers and the
children of the villagers.

15
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Sal bi sal, bavê Rêber genim dikelîne, piştî keland li ser
xênî radixe, piştî wê jî, dike dahn, dike savar, dike
qizrik, dike hûrik.
 
Year after year, Reber's father boils wheat, after boiling
it he spreads it on the roof, and after that, he makes
bulgur, makes savar, makes qizrik, makes hurik.

16
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Tiştên pir xweş çêdibin di gundê Baedîna da.
 
Very delicious things are made in the village of Baedina.

17
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Îro ji me re xwest ku em bi hev re derbasî cem xalê Mihemed
bibin.
 
Today we wanted to go together to Uncle Muhammad.

18
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Wekî her sal... kesên li qenala me temaşe dikin.
 
Just like every year... the people who watch our channel.

19
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Sala çûyî jî, em derbasî cem xalê Mihemed bûbûn.
 
Last year too, we had visited Uncle Muhammad.

20
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Lê îro, em ê dîsa derbasî cem xalê Mihemed bibin.
 
But today, we will visit Uncle Muhammad again.

21
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Em ê bi hev re temaşe bikin, niha wextê genim e, em ê bi hev
re rojeke Efrînî, xweş, derbas bikin di gundê Baedîna de, bi
silav û hurmet ji we re.
 
We will watch together, now is the wheat season, we will
spend a beautiful Afrin day together in the village of
Baedina, with greetings and respect to you.

22
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:48,000
De werin bi me re, û em ê temaşe bikin, em ê derbasî cem
xalê Mihemed bibin, de kerem bikin.
 
Come with us, and we will watch, we will visit Uncle
Muhammad, please come.

23
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Sibeh bi xêr.
 
Good morning.

24
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Xêr û selamet, ehlen û sehlan.
 
Goodness and safety, welcome.

25
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Elhemdulillah, tu çawa yî, siheta te çawa ye?
 
Praise be to God, how are you, how is your health?

26
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Elhemdulillah, baş e, xêr û selamet e.
 
Praise be to God, it is good, goodness and safety.

27
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Siheta te, xweş e? Te xebat kiriye? Wek her sal...
 
Your health, is it good? Have you been working? Like every
year...

28
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Welleh Xwedê ji milet razî be, û vê salê ha baran, ser milê
milet avêt, bi xêr be, sala çûyî jî...
 
By God, may God be pleased with the people, and this year
the rain fell on the people's shoulders, may it be blessed,
last year too...

29
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Salên çûn em...
 
The past years we...

30
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Derbas bûn çûn.
 
They passed and went.

31
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Û naha jî mewsima genim e bi xêr û selamet hat, me dest pê
kir.
 
And now it is also the wheat season, it arrived with
goodness and safety, we started.

32
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Xalê Mihemed wekî her sal, destpêkê vîdyoyê de me xeberda,
me got kesên nizanin, sala çûyî jî em derbasî cem xalê
Mihemed bibûn.
 
Uncle Muhammad, like every year, at the beginning of the
video we spoke, we said for those who don't know, last year
we had also visited Uncle Muhammad.

33
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Xalê Mihemed sal bi sal, li gundê Baedîna, yek ji kesên ku
bi destê xwe genim dikelîne...
 
Uncle Muhammad, year by year, in the village of Baedina, is
one of the people who boils the wheat with his own hands...

34
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Û bi destê xwe jî radixe, tu bi destê xwe dikşînî, paşê jî
tu diçî xênî, û tişt dikî, berê wî didî...
 
And with your own hands you spread it, you gather it with
your own hands, and then you go to the roof, and do things,
point it...

35
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Ez dixwazim am herin, am îsal... pirs bikin, genimê îsal
çawa ye, sal bixêr û bêr e, pir e?
 
I want us to go, let's ask about this year... how is this
year's wheat, is it a blessed and plentiful year, is there a
lot?

36
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Mewsima we çawa ye? Genim çawa ye, ew çi ye, rewşa wî çawa
ye?
 
How is your season? How is the wheat, what is it, how is its
situation?

37
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Welleh sal bixêr bû, baran xweş barî...
 
By God, the year was blessed, the rain fell well...

38
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Û genimê me rind e... û me dest pê kir... bi xêr û
selametî... me teqrîben...
 
And our wheat is good... and we started... with goodness and
safety... we approximately...

39
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Niha nêzîkî sê ton daxistin bixêr û selametî.
 
Now we brought down close to three tons with goodness and
safety.

40
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Bêje!
 
Say it!

41
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Asar jî... waneyên me... genim baş e.
 
This year too... our lessons... the wheat is good.

42
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Asar jî bihayê wî çawa ye, rind e?
 
This year too, how is its price, is it good?

43
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Welleh em çi bêjin... ji me re... dernaxe, yanî... mesrefa
xwe dernaxe.
 
By God what can we say... for us... it doesn't extract, I
mean... it doesn't cover its expenses.

44
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Teqrîben dibe derdora sî sentî ye... kîlo.
 
Approximately, it's around thirty cents... per kilo.

45
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Ev e, wekî tu dibînî... heqê radestî cotkaran e, û rêncberan
e...
 
This is it, as you see... the cost is delivered to the
farmers, and the laborers...

46
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Yekî dibêje em ê bi rê bin... em ê derxînin.
 
Someone says we will be on our way... we will extract it.

47
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Xalê Mihemed ev sîtla te dest pê kirî, ev a waciba çenda ye
te dikelîne?
 
Uncle Muhammad, this pot you've started, which batch is this
that you are boiling?

48
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Wacib teqrîben yê deha...
 
Batch approximately the tenth...

49
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Deha... ev a te...
 
The tenth... this is your...

50
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:35,000
A xaziran min kelandiye... ev a dehan e di nav sîtlê de.
 
I have boiled the ready ones... this is the tenth one in the
pot.

51
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Û her sîtelek, teqrîben, nîv çewal digre?
 
And each pot, approximately, takes half a sack?

52
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Belê, her sîtelek nîv çewal digre.
 
Yes, each pot takes half a sack.

53
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Naha her sîtelek nîv çewal digire... sibehê zû we kete
lêxist?
 
So each pot takes half a sack... did you start it early in
the morning?

54
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Ekseriye dibe êvarî, êvarî xêr e, lewma êvarî sî ye, yanî bê
germî mirov rehet radixe... û pê re belav dike.
 
Mostly it's in the evening, evening is better, because in
the evening it's shady, meaning without heat one spreads it
comfortably... and distributes it.

55
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Û milet jî, pak dibin, radibin, tevî xebatê, derdikevin
alîkariyê... Xwedê ji milet teva razî be... û teb'en, em jî,
eger yeke weke me hebe em ê jî alîkariya wî bikin.
 
And the people too, are clean, they get up, along with the
work, they come out to help... May God be pleased with all
the people... and naturally, we too, if there is someone
like us, we will help them too.

56
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Ev rubê... rojekî em jî dê herin rojekî ew ê alîkariya me
bikin.
 
This is the way... one day we will go, one day they will
help us.

57
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Xalê Mihemed, welleh te got biner, ev a dehan e.
 
Uncle Muhammad, by God you said look, this is the tenth one.

58
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

59
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Welleh min bawer nekir.
 
By God I didn't believe it.

60
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
De ha binêre.
 
Then look here.

61
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Welleh maşallah.
 
By God, may God bless it.

62
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Belê temaşevanên me yên hêja, wek hûn dibînin maşallah kelî.
 
Yes our dear viewers, as you can see, wow, it has boiled.

63
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Û genim jî pok e, Û Xalê Mihemed, sal bi sal çêdike.
 
And the wheat is clean too. And Uncle Muhammad, makes it
year after year.

64
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Kariyê, bi destê xwe gundiyan, pok e. Ser xênî gişkî pok
dikin.
 
The work, by his own hands and the villagers, is clean. They
clean the entire roof.

65
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Dikin ser kêfê, weke qaîdeyî, êdî ra dixe.
 
They do it with joy, as it is the rule, then he spreads it.

66
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Xalê Mihemed kom da xwestin, ez te re jî alîkar bikim,
yalla.
 
Uncle Muhammad, they asked to gather, let me help you too,
come on.

67
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Herin, alîkar bin, yalla.
 
Go ahead, help, come on.

68
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Ya Bismillah.
 
Oh, Bismillah.

69
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Erê wele, xêr, Bismillah.
 
Yes by God, good, Bismillah.

70
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Dilo wekî te digot, werin.
 
Dilo, like you were saying, come.

71
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Bê da çiqas zarok li me dabirin.
 
Come look how many children they gathered around us.

72
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Kê we tebîetê te jê re hiştiye, av jî nav o, tu tiştek nav
o.
 
Who left you this habit, there is no water in it, nothing in
it.

73
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Tê bîrî wekî kê ye, wî anî bi zarokan da bir.
 
Do you remember whose it is, he brought it and gave it to
the children.

74
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Germ e, maşallah.
 
It is hot, mashallah.

75
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Erê em piçûk bin çiqas em diçin dunyê, cîran e.
 
Yes, let us be small, however much we travel the world, it
is a neighbor.

76
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Mavê naxwaze?
 
Doesn't it need distance?

77
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Na na, mavê naxwaze bes li ser o.
 
No no, it doesn't need distance, just right on top of it.

78
00:10:41,000 --> 00:11:01,000
Yellah, heh.
 
Alright, here.

79
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Haa, tu çûyî ji kîjan alî ve hatî, gelo?
 
Ha, you went, from which side did you come back, I wonder?

80
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Erê... De vî alî ve biçe...
 
Yes... Then go from this side...

81
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

82
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Dinya jî germ e.
 
The weather is also warm.

83
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Wextê peliya ye, wextê orixa ye, wextê...
 
It's the time of leaves, the time of harvest, the time...

84
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Hemed! Zaro, kûçikê me te nedît bavo, sekinî me ko tu li
vir...
 
Hemed! Boy, didn't you see our dog father, I waited for you
here...

85
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,000
Erê xalê Mihemed.
 
Yes uncle Mihemed.

86
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Bixwedê ez ne şaş bim, here kefgîrekê bîne.
 
By God if I am not wrong, go bring a skimmer.

87
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Kefgîr jê vê re bîne.
 
Bring a skimmer from there for it.

88
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Çîçek te xwestkê?
 
Did you want a little one?

89
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Yellah... Heh.
 
Alright... Here.

90
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Xalê Mihemed em ra go, gotim o no nav e ru, rabe we re tişta
jê re ke...
 
Uncle Mihemed told us, I said that's not its name, get up
and make something for it...

91
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Ax ka fît germ e? Te çawa destê xwe kirê?
 
Ah is it very hot? How did you put your hand in it?

92
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Destê te naşewite?
 
Does your hand not burn?

93
00:14:55,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Xwedê te'ala tu caran me girê nede... Xwedê bereketê têxe...
 
May God Almighty never tie us up... May God put blessing in
it...

94
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Germ e? Têk çû ke. Tîşkî bîne ke.
 
Is it hot? Put it down. Bring a little and put it in.

95
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Xalê Mihemed em ragihî, gotim a we ne, raxwe jor...
 
Uncle Mihemed informed us, I said this is it, spread it
up...

96
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Manî av li bin da me, hewa jî vena da ber da...
 
Meaning the water is under us, the air also blew down like
this...

97
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Xwe berda kê nekşîne? Giran e belê.
 
Who didn't pull themselves down? It's heavy, yes.

98
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Xalo teme heye? Na teme heye...
 
Uncle, do you have a wish/greed? No, do you have...

99
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Na tam e me na, manî em narjîn e.
 
No, we don't have greed, meaning we don't spill it.

100
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Oya, ehlen we sehlen...
 
Oh, welcome...

101
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Selamet be ser milet tev da. Xêr û selamet...
 
May there be safety on the whole nation. Good and safety...

102
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Xêr, bereket e. Ev mehşera îsal e. Dema li kelê kefe...
 
Good, it is a blessing. This is the harvest of this year.
When it comes to a boil...

103
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Xêrê jê bibînin. A ev a we re rind bîne, darê dixe tê de
dakele.
 
May they see good from it. Bring this well for yourself, put
wood in it and it boils.

104
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Sala par ceribî. Ba de me keland deranî, em dander dişkên,
dido ro ya sê, em ber dikin...
 
Last year it was tested. After we boiled it and took it out,
we crack the wheat, for two or three days, we lay it out...

105
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Heta huşk bibe, hedî hedî...
 
Until it dries, slowly slowly...

106
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Em radikin.
 
We lift it.

107
00:16:40,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Û derdixin çala.
 
And take it out to the pit.

108
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Rê dikin. Û rexistine şûn de, wexta heta mesela sibe de,
sibê em ê dîsa...
 
We lay it out. And after laying it out, until for example
tomorrow, tomorrow we will again...

109
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Heta huşk bibe, em ê rakin, cîhê xo pak bive.
 
Until it dries, we will take it, make its place clean.

110
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Ev jî ziyad bî badî du roj a şûn da em ê têkin tûr.
 
This too, when it's plenty, after two days we will put it in
bags.

111
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Kû wê re wa qesta aş be em ê bavêjin.
 
When it is ready like that, straight to the mill we will
throw it.

112
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Ha vo temam ê huşk bûyî ye.
 
This is the one completely dried.

113
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:42,000
Ê huşk bûyî, em ê rakin.
 
The dried one, we will pick it up.

114
00:17:42,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Û dest pê rohazir bikin.
 
And start preparing it.

115
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Kê neha genim da şûn?
 
Who just put the wheat back?

116
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Bes dayîka Rêber razî nabe wekî ew dernekeve. Em derxînin...
 
But Rêber's mother doesn't agree to uncover it. So let's
uncover it...

117
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Em hatin ko me derxist. Em qet derxînin.
 
We came to uncover it. We should just uncover it.

118
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
De kerem ke derxîne.
 
Please, go ahead and uncover it.

119
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Ev genimê ko pê hatiye kelandin.
 
This is the wheat that has been boiled.

120
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
De qey genim te çend ava te şûştin?
 
So how many times did you wash the wheat with water?

121
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Du ava. Du ava.
 
With two waters. With two waters.

122
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Wê ava berî tu genim kelînî te şûşt e...
 
The water that you washed the wheat with before boiling
it...

123
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Ê, bo genim pak be tê şûştin, şûştina wî baş e.
 
Yes, it is washed so the wheat is clean, washing it is good.

124
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Bismîlah ev genimê te ye, a qedehek bo min têr e.
 
Bismillah, this is your wheat, a bowl is enough for me.

125
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,000
Vê berikî ji bo te avêtibû ser? Ev berik...
 
What did you put this cover over it for? This cover...

126
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Ev ji bo hilmê wê negre, germiya wê negre...
 
This is so it doesn't lose its steam, so it doesn't lose its
heat...

127
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:02,000
Baş e te teqan li ser daye û çend saetan genim di nav da di
hêle?
 
Good, you put a cover on it, and how many hours do you leave
the wheat inside?

128
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Sê saetan, sê saet nîv em dihêlin.
 
Three hours, three and a half hours we leave it.

129
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Gellekî baş e... Xalê Mihemed tu karî hinekî bes hinekî min
re baxivî?
 
Very good... Uncle Mihemed, could you please just talk to me
a little?

130
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Xêra te genim hin caran tirş dibe. Xalê Mihemed ew genim ji
çi tirş dibe?
 
Please, sometimes wheat gets sour. Uncle Mihemed, why does
that wheat get sour?

131
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Ew e tu qet nexin nav hev... eger yek cî de bimîne tirş
dibe.
 
That is when you pile it up together... if it stays in one
place, it gets sour.

132
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:43,000
Tu pê gelek pahn nakî tirş dibe... ger pahn ke ew wekî pahn
bû tirş nabe.
 
If you don't spread it wide, it gets sour... if you spread
it, once it is spread it won't get sour.

133
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Eger tu baş wê pahn bike genim genim tirş nabe...
 
If you spread it well, the wheat won't get sour...

134
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Destpêkê bo kelandina genim dayîka Rêber me re qal kir ku
hûn çawa dişon... ava paqij.
 
In the beginning for boiling the wheat, Rêber's mother told
us how you wash it... with clean water.

135
00:21:54,000 --> 00:22:00,000
Û hûn dixin nav qazanan û ava paqij berdidin ser. Û hûn agir
binda dikin.
 
And you put it in pots and pour clean water over it. And you
light a fire under it.

136
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Çend saetan ew dixwaze li ser êgir bimîne da ku bikelî?
 
How many hours does it need to stay on the fire to boil?

137
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:12,000
Ê teb'en nêzîkî sê saetan li ser agir dihele.
 
Yes, of course, it stays on the fire for nearly three hours.

138
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:19,000
Li gora êgir e... ku tu qels agir bidî, agirî kêm tu bidî,
de sê saet û nîv bidome.
 
It depends on the fire... if you give a weak fire, if you
give a low fire, it will take three and a half hours.

139
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:24,000
Tu agirê xurt jî bidî e... êdî gerê agir baş bê.
 
And if you give a strong fire... well, the fire must be
good.

140
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Çunkî tu genim bi êgir kelînî, gerê tu qels nekin, eger qels
bê de genim xera be.
 
Because you boil wheat with fire, you shouldn't make it
weak, if it's weak the wheat will get ruined.

141
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:37,000
Xêr û bereketa reb ul-alemîn da dibe zêde û di pir dibe...
 
The blessings and abundance of the Lord of the worlds will
increase it and it becomes plentiful...

142
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:42,000
Û îcbarî genimagir xurt bê, ku tu agir kêm keyî xera dibe.
 
And it's obligatory for the wheat fire to be strong, if you
lower the fire it gets ruined.

143
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:48,000
Sê saet û nîv nêzîk e heya de kelî û xilas be.
 
Almost three and a half hours until it boils and finishes.

144
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Ev e derket holê ku hûn ê bikelînin. Piştî kelî te ew
daxist, wisa ye?
 
It turns out that you will boil it. After it boiled, you
took it down, right?

145
00:22:53,000 --> 00:23:00,000
E erê... eger kelî, em daxin. Bêguman... em di rûtin ser ew
kuncî an ser ciyek paqij...
 
Yes... if it boiled, we take it down. Of course... we pour
it onto the sacks or onto a clean place...

146
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Teqrîben sê rub'an av jê dimîne.
 
Approximately three quarters of the water remains from it.

147
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Sê rub'an av em li de derdixin û kom dikin...
 
Three quarters of the water we take out and pile it...

148
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:13,000
Û paşê tu bala xwe bidê, ev deştîyê, cîran, malbat êdî me de
kom bûn.
 
And then you pay attention, these folks, neighbors, family
gathered with us.

149
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Ji nêzîk û ji dûr e û em ji bo xwe jî em nedin.
 
From near and from far and for ourselves we do not give.

150
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Ev heqê miletê ye em tiştek jê nedin... me nafroşe e... me
ew heqê xwe jî bidayê.
 
This is the people's right, we don't give any of it... we
don't sell it... we gave our own share to it too.

151
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Çavê te bi gundiyan dikeve ev amade dibin. Sahet xweş ji bo
hemiyan be.
 
You set your eyes on the villagers, they get ready. Good
health to all of them.

152
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Kî de bixwe... xêr û bereket be ji wî mirovî re...
 
Whoever will eat... may it be blessings and abundance for
that person...

153
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:41,000
Bi rastî xalê Mihemed, di zemanê berê da... mirov...
 
Truthfully Uncle Mihemed, in the past times... people...

154
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:44,000
Berê pirtir malan di kelandin... gellek... di kelandin, me
dît pir çuwal dikelandin.
 
In the past more houses boiled... a lot... they boiled, we
saw they boiled many sacks.

155
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Niha çima wisa kêm bûye... Xalê Mihemed ev yek?
 
Why has it decreased like this now... Uncle Mihemed, this
thing?

156
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:55,000
E teb'en... berê mirov ko di kelandin di çandin... ew fîqar
bûn.
 
Yes of course... in the past people who boiled also
planted... they were poor.

157
00:23:55,000 --> 00:24:02,000
E çuwal di kelandin e mala te ko çuwal ne kelînî nabe mal.
 
They boiled sacks, your house if it didn't boil sacks it
wasn't a house.

158
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:10,000
Mirov fîqar bûn... te got ko yeka de du çuwal... an du sê
mal di bûn. Waliyê gundan yeko yek e.
 
People were poor... you'd say one had two sacks... or two
three houses were together. The state of the villages was
all the same.

159
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:17,000
Berê mirov... yek çuwal dudu dikelandin. E wîlayeta mala
wisa mezin bûn...
 
In the past people... boiled one or two sacks. The capacity
of the houses was big like that...

160
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:22,000
Îro kulfet heye, sê, çar çuwal de kelînin jiber e.
 
Today there is family, they boil three, four sacks because
of it.

161
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Û e kêm bûye... tişt...
 
And it has decreased... the thing...

162
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:31,000
Xalê Mihemed ez ji we tiştekî bipirsim... wê dera tu lê
rûdiniştî min dît te gelek paqij kirîbû berî e bibe.
 
Uncle Mihemed, let me ask you something... that place you
were sitting, I saw you had cleaned it a lot before it
happened.

163
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:33,000
Ev dibêjin çi, navê çi lê dikin?
 
What do they call this, what name do they give it?

164
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:35,000
Ciyê endarê... endarê.
 
It's the threshing place... the threshing floor.

165
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:38,000
Ew gundê te, mintiqa te gundê çi ye?
 
That village of yours, your region is what village?

166
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:41,000
Mintiqa min a efrînê ye, mintiqa endarê ye...
 
My region is Efrin's, the threshing region...

167
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Berî... bi salan, bi zeman, da ew qet çuwal te ne kelandine?
 
In the past... for years, in those times, did you ever not
boil any sacks?

168
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Çima em nikelînin... teb'en em de kelînin ew zemana ew e ew
mîrasa... kal û bavan.
 
Why wouldn't we boil... of course we boil, that time is the
inheritance of... ancestors.

169
00:24:54,000 --> 00:25:03,000
Ev sal bi sal de kelînin... ew adetên me de çu car xera
nabe... ew wisa berekete... ew tişt...
 
This year by year we boil... our traditions never get
ruined... it's a blessing like that... that thing...

170
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:07,000
Hêdî hêdî de çêke, te bi dila...
 
Slowly it gets done, to your heart's content...

171
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:12,000
Tu de xêrê bî tu de xweşî yê bî...
 
May you be in goodness, may you be in happiness...

172
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:19,000
Min pirsyek din jî eger çêbibe... cûreyê vî genimî çi ye ko
tu di kelînî? Cûreyê wî çi ye?
 
I have another question if possible... what is the type of
this wheat you are boiling? What is its type?

173
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:22,000
Cûreyê genim?
 
The type of wheat?

174
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:29,000
Vî genimî navê wî sorîk e ko di kelînî em berî jê re digot.
Derece yekê ye...
 
The name of this wheat is Sorik that you are boiling, we
used to say that in the past. It's first degree...

175
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:33,000
Berê pir habûn, niha cûreyê xwe nemaye.
 
It used to be plentiful, now its type doesn't exist anymore.

176
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:35,000
Niha ya qeysî ye qeysî...
 
Now it's the Qeysi one, Qeysi...

177
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:38,000
Ev qeysî ye, em vî di kelînin.
 
This is Qeysi, we boil this one.

178
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:43,000
Ev cûre bo dan e. Yê Qeysî ye ew de kelînin. E ya bilxur ê.
 
This kind is for pounded wheat. It's Qeysi, we boil that
one. Yes, it's for bulgur.

179
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:52,000
Û ew genim eynî cûreyê tovim e ku hûn di çînin, cûre ne yek
e? Cûreyê tova yê ku nexweşe yê çandê?
 
And is that wheat the exact same kind of seed that you
plant, or are the types not the same? The seed type that you
plant?

180
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:58,000
Na na ew eynî ye qeysî. Bes eger cûreyekî dîn bê yê ko şil û
xirab e ev cûreyê dî... nake tovim.
 
No, no it's the same, Qeysi. But if it's another kind that
is soft and bad, this other kind... it won't make a seed.

181
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:05,000
Ew yekî dî ye ko dibe bilxur û genim, yê bilxur a û yê te dî
yê qeysî ye...
 
That is another one that becomes bulgur and wheat, the one
for bulgur and the one you saw is Qeysi...

182
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Da ez pirseke din kim de... te wê avê bi ser ve di kî kîjan
av de tu bi ser ve dî di avê dî bikelînî an eynî ava nû yî
paqij de xê?
 
Let me ask another question... that water you pour over it,
which water do you pour, do you boil the other water or do
you put the same new clean water?

183
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:22,000
Ev ê adetê me qet... ew kal û bav ne wisa dikirin em jî wê
ava nû ya paqij di din. Ew yeka qet em... me di rût ew yek e
dî av... we dît em te dî av de paqij av e.
 
This is our tradition never... our ancestors used to do it
like this and we also give it the new clean water. That one
we just... we poured out that other water... you saw we put
clean water again.

184
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:27,000
Xalê Mihemed tu bala xwe de di pir dera da... min di dît
berya niha ew ava te rûtî yê germ...
 
Uncle Mihemed if you pay attention in many places... I used
to see before that hot water you poured...

185
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:33,000
Ew ava we, de ber da ordekê, da berda heywanê wisa te de min
dîtin ew çî bûn ew we di firotin?
 
That water of yours, you gave it to ducks, you gave it to
animals like that I saw, what were those, did you sell them?

186
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:40,000
E wela ez de bo te bêjim ew tişt e ko hinek ew de firotin,
ew em ne de firoştin me ne meyl e ev tişt...
 
Ah by God let me tell you that thing is that some would sell
them, we wouldn't sell them, we have no inclination for this
thing...

187
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:45,000
Em me didin heywanên xwe... wek ku te te dî e didin kuçik û
teyran û pez em ew didin pêz...
 
We would give it to our animals... like what you saw they
give to dogs and birds and sheep, we give it to sheep...

188
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Tu de xêrê û de saetê de bî... e baş...
 
May you be in goodness and health... well...

189
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:53,000
Xalê Mihemed, wekî dayîka Rêber de min pirsî e hinek tişt da
pirse min da...
 
Uncle Mihemed, like I asked Rêber's mother, there's
something else I have to ask...

190
00:26:53,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Genim, car car eger ku wisa tirş dibe... yanî tu çawa dizanî
e ku ew tirş dibe, guneh e tu karî rûn bikî min re?
 
Wheat, sometimes if it gets sour like that... I mean how do
you know if it gets sour, it's a shame, can you explain to
me?

191
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Ê... ew tirş dibe eger te wê wisa ko qurm de te de kom ki ew
ava te de ser de e e qeys mezin de av tê... ew ava wek ku
germ... ew yek bi yek dibe heya kî hilmê da we rûtin nav hev
da...
 
Yes... it gets sour if you just pile it up at the base and
that water you put over it... a large amount of water
comes... that water since it's hot... it mixes one by one
until the steam falls into it together...

192
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:23,000
De ev ew tîşte ko deke genim bibe tirş e, ew ser... di
bandora genim dike.
 
And this is the thing that makes the wheat get sour, that
over... it impacts the wheat.

193
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Wisa ne... û bilxur ji te'm e de xera nabe an hema wisa xera
de be?
 
Is that so... and does the bulgur's taste not get ruined or
does it just get ruined like that?

194
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:44,000
E teb'en ew wisa ku tirş dibe ew genim hema wisa xera dibe
di qede e te'ma we xerab be te'ma wê xerab dike ew ko tirş
dibe eger kêm av e kêm av rûtê.
 
Yes of course, when it gets sour like that, the wheat just
gets ruined like that, it perishes, its taste gets ruined,
it ruins its taste when it gets sour if less water, you pour
less water.

195
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Tu genim rûtin ewe pahn ke yan tu qet wisa weke e cî de
nehêle te wê pahn kî. Tu pahn ki tirş nabe qet yeko yê xera
nabe... tu de rûtin ser wisa heya xilas dibe de rûtin nav...
ev e de.
 
When you pour wheat, spread it or don't just leave it in one
place, you should spread it. If you spread it, it won't get
sour at all, none of it will get ruined... you'll pour it
out until it's finished and pour it in... here it is.

196
00:27:51,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Temaşevanên me yî hêja ev car e de em xwişkeke min di ser
masincer ew de me xeber da ez wekî tu raqemê xalê Mihemed
bide yê.
 
Our dear viewers, this time our sister on Messenger spoke to
us so I could give you Uncle Mihemed's number.

197
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Wê pirsê ko genim de keland ew me pir de xweş bûn e de genim
de qeland de çêdikî...
 
Her question about the wheat boiling was that we liked it a
lot that you boil wheat and prepare it...

198
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:15,000
Ez de bo min bo vî yê teqez de niha raqema babê Rêber da de
ji terê û ko em ko... ko ciyek we derket ko wisa nêzîk da
min jî teqez de Xalê Mihemed dî em ji wî dî da wî der de de
wî çê de pirsîn.
 
I will definitely give Rêber's father's number to you now
and if... if a place like that came up nearby, I definitely
saw Uncle Mihemed and we would ask him about that place.

199
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:18,000
Da tu e tenê da vî de kelînî? Tê derxe hinek re na?
 
Will you only boil this? Will you bring it out for someone
else?

200
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:24,000
Ne. Ez... ew bo min û mal û ko dî sê mal dî ko ew me sê mal
hene ev. Em ji e de derxistin e. Ev bo me ye bo genim der de
ew yek de kelîn e... ev de kêm nabe ev hene ew de kelîn.
 
No. I... it's for me and my house and the other three
houses, we have three houses. We brought it out. It's for us
for the wheat to boil... this won't decrease, there is more
to boil.

201
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:33,000
Xalê Mihemed te dît me ev zarok ev de... ew me gelek me pirs
dikirin heta ko me zarok me ji bîr dikirin min te dî min ji
bîr dikirin qey min ew genim ev tiştek me ew me çiqas xwest?
 
Uncle Mihemed you saw these children... they were asking us
a lot until we forgot the children, I saw you I forgot did
I... did we ask for that wheat, for this thing?

202
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:35,000
E. E...
 
Yes. Yes...

203
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:44,000
Ez sipasiyek mezin dikim ji tera tu herdem sax de saetê de
yî em te di xwaze bereketê. Xwedê rizqê te ev wisa zêde bike
û ev me ew e genim ev di kelîn û de nexe qet ew de zêde bike
bereket de bîn.
 
I give you a big thank you, may you always be healthy, we
wish you blessings. May God increase your provision like
this and this wheat we boil won't perish, it will increase
and bring blessing.

204
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:49,000
E wela wisa tu sax be tu qenciyê bike... em qet xêr nabîn e
ji bo e kanala we yî yê te qenciyê bîne.
 
Yes by God, may you be healthy, may you do goodness... we've
seen nothing but good from your channel that brings you
goodness.

205
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Silavan de hemû ev milletê Kurdê em her her be silav.
 
Greetings to all this Kurdish nation, we always send
greetings.

206
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:58,000
Em li hebe derek tu yî em de e wisa xweş bin wî te yî kîdera
tu bî e xweş silavan de we...
 
Wherever you are, we'll be happy like this, wherever you
are, happy greetings to you...

207
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Bo ew mêvan bî ko bo zarokan em de wî nêzîk de dî me ev. Wî
silavan.
 
Be a guest for the children, we will see you closely.
Greetings.

208
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:15,000
Tu de silavan de xweş bî Temaşevanên me yî hêja ev wisa e ev
di ev ko ez we de vîdyo yê te em pir de spasiyê de bîn ew ji
bo ko te bo me ev yek heye ji min bo te yî de spasiye bî.
 
May your greetings be happy, our dear viewers, like this, in
this video I thank you very much because you have this for
us, I thank you.

209
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:23,000
Ev wê ez spasiya da di bavê Rêber yî wek wî ko wî wisa ev ko
te nîne sal bi sal di wisa ew kar qet nîne ew ev...
 
And I will thank Rêber's father like that because he doesn't
have it, year by year like that, there's no work like
this...

210
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:35,000
Em ew spasiyek wisa wî milletî afrîn bo bavê Rêber bo me wek
ko ew nîne bo wî. Û wî ko ew em wek tişt nî bo wan wekî me
ev silav ji wan dî dît bo ko wî wisa nîne me nizanîn wê der.
 
We send such a thanks to the people of Efrin for Rêber's
father, because he doesn't have it for him. And because we
didn't have anything like it for them, we received these
greetings from them because we didn't know about that place.

211
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:47,000
Te wisa de wisa ko silavan bo milletê ew te rehma wî ya wî
efrîn wî nî ko te der e em wisa. Bo me ew e wisa ko tu yî de
wan. Em silavan de ko ev wisa ev te de bo milet e Kurd ko
der e wek te ko ew e.
 
Just like that, greetings to the nation, his mercy of Efrin
who went there, we are like that. For us it's like that
where you are for them. We send greetings to the Kurdish
nation who is there like you.

212
00:29:47,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Tu de sax bî...
 
May you be healthy...

213
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:20,000
[Mûzîka Gelêrî]
 
[Traditional Music]

214
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:45,000
[Mûzîka Govendê]
 
